WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.793 --> 00:00:03.293
(eerie music)

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.039
- When the young kids on the street

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:09.005
found out that I was working on Star Wars,

00:00:09.005 --> 00:00:11.088
I was like a God to them.

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:13.466
(droid beeping)

00:00:13.466 --> 00:00:16.154
Those kids are now parents.

00:00:16.154 --> 00:00:19.965
They've seen the movies
throughout the years.

00:00:19.965 --> 00:00:21.296
It was always in the
back of their mind, like,

00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:23.689
"Oh, I remember playing with the Falcon,

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.987
"I remember playing with the
X-wing and the TIE fighter."

00:00:25.987 --> 00:00:27.233
(Vader breathing)

00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:28.126
(lightsaber whooshing)

00:00:28.126 --> 00:00:31.003
To understand that you have a small part

00:00:31.003 --> 00:00:34.670
of that kind of bigger
world is pretty cool.

00:00:36.615 --> 00:00:40.103
(exciting music)

00:00:40.103 --> 00:00:41.665
My name is Mark Boudreaux,

00:00:41.665 --> 00:00:43.239
and I've been fortunate enough

00:00:43.239 --> 00:00:46.460
to work on Star Wars toys since 1977.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.826
(upbeat music)

00:00:49.826 --> 00:00:51.400
The amazing thing about Star Wars,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.185
I don't think it's really ever gone away.

00:00:53.185 --> 00:00:55.102
It's always been there.

00:00:56.031 --> 00:00:59.019
Vehicles has been sort of what I really am

00:00:59.019 --> 00:01:00.813
the most passionate about:

00:01:00.813 --> 00:01:03.896
TIE fighters, X-wings, Rey's speeder.

00:01:07.849 --> 00:01:11.095
I have always built
models, built planes, cars,

00:01:11.095 --> 00:01:13.759
so they said, "Hey, Mark,
why don't you go ahead

00:01:13.759 --> 00:01:16.019
and start working on
the Millennium Falcon?"

00:01:16.019 --> 00:01:18.681
I said like, "Sure, why not?"

00:01:18.681 --> 00:01:22.323
(drum and bass music)

00:01:22.323 --> 00:01:25.616
The Millennium Falcon is
more than just a machine.

00:01:25.616 --> 00:01:28.587
It really is a character
that helps save the day.

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:31.678
It's more than just a hunk of junk.

00:01:31.678 --> 00:01:34.197
You want it to be able
to provide an experience

00:01:34.197 --> 00:01:36.776
that could extend from the film,

00:01:36.776 --> 00:01:39.142
so when you went to go see the movie,

00:01:39.142 --> 00:01:41.049
you come right back and
you're playing with Luke,

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:43.238
you're playing with Han,
you're playing with Chewie,

00:01:43.238 --> 00:01:44.836
and you're able to relive everything

00:01:44.836 --> 00:01:46.919
that you saw in the film.

00:01:47.928 --> 00:01:50.305
(soft music)

00:01:50.305 --> 00:01:54.114
Long after I've gone to the
Force, wherever that might be,

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.864
this product will still be there.

00:01:58.116 --> 00:02:01.027
Grandkids from now will hopefully

00:02:01.027 --> 00:02:03.131
still be enjoying Star Wars.

00:02:03.131 --> 00:02:05.272
And we certainly want to
try to do our small part

00:02:05.272 --> 00:02:08.355
into making sure that that continues.

